  "notes": "Registration and type need FAA confirmation (see icao_hex/type check). FAA: Boeing 737-8 (MAX 8). Drawn from N945WN, which still wore Florida One in April 2026 (Commons, BWI). airframes/SWA.json lists N9019R as the current Florida One from Wikipedia, with no photo found; whether the scheme has moved, or N9019R carries the same design, is not confirmed. The seal (its ring, lettering and scene) is a logo, apps draw it as art; re-measured 2026-11-28 on the January 2019 left photo of N945WN, the right side from the April 2026 right photo: the scene mirrored with the woman forward on both sides, the ring's lettering reading the same way round ('STATE OF' aft, 'FLORIDA' forward on the right). The seal's lower aft quarter is behind the wing and engine in every side photo. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the fin is the state jets' Heart fin as re-measured on Colorado One (the same fin on every 737), copied with its 'Southwest' title and flag. 'Florida One' measured on the April 2026 right-side photo of N945WN against the nose and the forward door (2.5-3.4 m back), two weights, a pair of titles per side (the left side mirrored), on Colorado One's line under the cockpit windows. The seal's circles made smooth. Drawn on the 737-700 (N945WN); on the 737-8 N9019R the art sits at the same metres, so a little further forward as shares.",
  "history": "Previously N945WN (737-700, 2010)."
}
